                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The home care nurse is visiting a client who was recently diagnosed with a hearing impairment. The nurse would prepare to instruct the client's spouse in which measure that will facilitate communication?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nMeasures that facilitate hearing in the client with a hearing impairment include speaking in a normal tone, avoiding shouting, talking directly to the client while facing the client, and speaking clearly. If the client does not seem to understand what is said, the statement needs to be expressed differently. Moving closer to the client and toward the better ear may facilitate communication, but talking directly into the impaired ear needs to be avoided.",
                        "id": "2ae5e29a9b5c4bd5ae626bad3844bcb1",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
